WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.140
Mark Hamill has been a household name for
decades, and while his name's become synonymous

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.170
with Star Wars' Luke Skywalker - undoubtedly
his best-known role - there's a lot more to

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.480
the actor than the moisture farmer turned
space wizard he's so often conflated with.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.660
One area in which Mark Hamill and Skywalker
are remarkably similar is in their definitively

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.640
unglamorous upbringings.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.900
Though Hamill didn't grow up as the son of
farmers on a desert planet, he was the fourth

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.090
of seven children, all of whom were ushered
from location to location as their father

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:34.240
was stationed in various places as a U.S.
Navy captain.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.760
Though Hamill had the exciting opportunity
to live in Japan for part of his youth, that

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.780
didn't prevent him from starting his acting
career like so many bright-eyed young people:

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.420
working at a fast food restaurant and racking
up smaller roles.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.080
In fact, Hamill was even fired from his job
at a Jack in the Box restaurant for doing

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:56.040
too good an impression of the chain's mascot
character as patrons used the drive-thru window.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.240
"My manager didn't think it was very funny.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.880
He told me to go home and never come back."

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.620
“Wow.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.520
Fired from Jack in the Box?”

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.970
"Fired for being in character!”

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:09.470
This, of course, proved early on that he had
a knack for voicing kooky clowns - a skill

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:12.340
that would come in handy a couple decades
down the line.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.920
Though Luke Skywalker was his breakout role,
Hamill had actually been acting since at least

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.240
1963, when he took on a small role in the
wildly popular soap opera General Hospital.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.780
He continued to have brief on-screen roles
in TV hits of the day, including The Bill

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.920
Cosby Show and The Partridge Family.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.920
Things went on in this fashion for some time,
with Hamill finally landing a few recurring

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.560
characters on The New Scooby-Doo Movies, Jeannie,
and The Texas Wheelers.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.020
So while he wasn't on the fast track to stardom
right upon his arrival in Los Angeles, he

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.280
was certainly putting in the work and building
up a substantial portfolio, something he could

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.800
present to George Lucas to seal his fate for
the rest of his life.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.640
Luke Skywalker was a lucky break, but Hamill
was a hard-working kid, proving that destiny

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.780
isn't the only factor in achieving stardom.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.440
In order to combat the typecasting that would
inevitably result from his portrayal as the

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:12.530
wide-eyed, young hero of destiny Luke Skywalker,
Hamill branched out into other forms of acting.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.260
First, as many young actors do, he spent a
brief stint in the early '80s working in Broadway

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.000
plays like The Elephant Man and Amadeus.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.760
He followed this endeavor with a dive headfirst
into voice acting.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.730
As noted earlier, his penchant for impressions
and silly voices would only aid him further

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.950
in his career.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:34.030
His keen interest in comic books helped to
land him the role of the Joker in the beloved

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:40.170
cartoon Batman: The Animated Series, but Hamill
has done work outside cartoons as well, diving

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.860
into the video game industry as a voice artist.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.200
"Surprise!

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:51.160
You fell for the old sick Joker gag, Batman!"

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:56.280
Naturally, some of these roles are reprisals
of his work in the Star Wars and Batman franchises,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:02.320
but his first video game voice opportunity
came in 1993, in the mystery thriller

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.300
Gabriel Knight: Sins of the Fathers.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.860
He's portrayed characters in several sci-fi
military-themed games, like the Wing Commander

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:14.640
series, and one wonders if he was able to
pull from his experience growing up on naval bases.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.180
It's no secret that Hamill is a comic book
fan - and thank goodness, too, considering

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.660
he appears at one comic convention after another
to the delight of his adoring fans.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.360
But Hamill has also had a hand in writing
some comics of his own.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.580
In the mid-'90s, right before the Star Wars
prequel films, Hamill co-authored

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.640
The Black Pearl with his cousin Eric Johnson.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.740
The comic, featuring art by H.M. Baker and
published by Dark Horse, was a five-issue

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.720
series intended to be collected into one volume
at the end of its run.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.980
It follows Luther Drake, who inadvertently
prevents an abduction and continues to pursue

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.730
a life of nighttime vigilantism.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.810
Sounds a bit like Batman, doesn't it?

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:00.290
But it's the post-Frank Miller type of Batman,
dark and conflicted and morally ambiguous.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:05.190
The comic was originally written as a screenplay,
and as recently as 2010, Hamill still had

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:10.140
intentions to see this dark vision brought
to life onscreen with himself in the director's chair.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:15.320
While part of Hamill's online presence is
populated by his political thoughts, he's

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.400
also dedicated a decent chunk of it to interacting
with fans.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:24.319
He continues to have the most delightful knack
for self-deprecating humor and a genuine gratitude

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:28.539
for the fans who have supported him from the
beginning - or even those newer fans who have

00:04:28.539 --> 00:04:31.960
come to Star Wars with the newest installments
of the franchise.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.800
He spends a lot of his tweeting energy singing
the praises of his fellow actors, promoting

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.700
Star Wars-related news, and sharing stories
of his friendships with the likes of the late,

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.660
adored Carrie Fisher.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.600
Hamill is a savvy Twitter user, in other words.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:51.580
Social media certainly has its problems, but
with 3.2 million followers, it's safe to say

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.000
the Force is with him when it comes to interacting
with his audience.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.520
Hamill has been married to his wife, dental
hygienist Marilou York, since 1978, not long

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.569
after the release of A New Hope.

00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:09.330
The couple have three children and one grandchild,
and seem to have successfully avoided a lot

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.120
of the typical drama that Hollywood couples
tend to fall into.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:17.420
Hamill and York's long, happy marriage is
often attributed to York's lack of celebrity.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:21.659
They broke up for a period so Hamill could
get the rush of stardom out of his system,

00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:24.839
but in the end, family and stability won out.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.920
By marrying a non-celebrity, Hamill wasn't
competing with all of Hollywood's other leading

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:34.760
men, and he married her not for her star power
or her paparazzi appeal, but because they

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.080
had a genuine connection.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.540
No doubt the two have worked very hard at
keeping their relationship alive, but it is

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:45.129
clear that they still love each other very
much, and it is gratifying to see such a healthy

00:05:45.129 --> 00:05:49.389
marriage flourish even as Hamill has returned
to the Hollywood limelight with the final

00:05:49.389 --> 00:05:52.620
installments of the Star Wars franchise's
Skywalker saga.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:58.540
Despite the concerns about being typecast,
Hamill has done an excellent job of proving

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:02.379
he can have a satisfying and successful career
outside Star Wars.

00:06:02.379 --> 00:06:07.419
So as the torch is passed from Luke to Rey,
we see Hamill continuing in much the same

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:08.710
manner as usual.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:13.889
He dons the animated white face of the Joker
time and again in various new animated DC

00:06:13.889 --> 00:06:18.140
series, and makes guest appearances on TV
series like The Big Bang Theory.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.580
"Hi."

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.900
"I'm gonna need a minute."

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.159
But some roles and projects stand out more
than others.

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:35.720
He put his villainous voice to good use as
the devious doll Chucky in the 2019 film Child's

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:40.919
Play before taking the role of the Scientist
in The Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance, the

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:46.180
long-hyped prequel to Jim Henson's 1982 cult
classic puppet-fueled fantasia.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:51.060
Continuing his long appreciation for the comics
medium, he's also taken a role in Amazon's

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:56.620
adaptation of Robert Kirkman, Cory Walker,
and Ryan Ottley's Invincible, which chronicles

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.940
the life of the son of a superhero.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:03.499
Still in the spotlight after all these years,
Mark Hamill has proven he has the talent to

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:07.700
tackle a wide variety of roles - and we can't
wait to see what he does next.

